      "id": "t1", "accountId": "a2", "mailboxIds": ["a2-inbox", "a2-projects-inboxed"],
      "subject": "Inboxed design review: sidebar and thread view", "unread": true,
      "messages": [
        { "id": "m1", "minutesAgo": 2880, "from": { "name": "Maya Chen", "email": "maya@work.example" },
          "to": [{ "name": "You", "email": "you@work.example" }, { "name": "Daniel Okafor", "email": "daniel@work.example" }],
          "body": "Hi both,\n\nI've pushed the first pass of the sidebar and the thread view to the design file. The sidebar follows the reference we liked: an icon rail for accounts, then the mailbox tree with thin guide lines for nested folders.\n\nCould you take a look before Thursday?\n\nMaya" },
        { "id": "m2", "minutesAgo": 1440, "from": { "name": "Daniel Okafor", "email": "daniel@work.example" },
          "to": [{ "name": "Maya Chen", "email": "maya@work.example" }, { "name": "You", "email": "you@work.example" }],
          "body": "Looks great. One question: do we show unread counts on every folder or only the inbox?\n\nOn Tue, Maya Chen wrote:\n> Could you take a look before Thursday?" },
        { "id": "m3", "minutesAgo": 1200, "from": { "name": "You", "email": "you@work.example" },
          "to": [{ "name": "Maya Chen", "email": "maya@work.example" }, { "name": "Daniel Okafor", "email": "daniel@work.example" }],
          "body": "Every folder, but only the inbox count gets the accent colour. Everything else stays muted so the inbox reads first.\n\nOn Wed, Daniel Okafor wrote:\n> do we show unread counts on every folder or only the inbox?" },
        { "id": "m4", "minutesAgo": 35, "from": { "name": "Maya Chen", "email": "maya@work.example" },
          "to": [{ "name": "You", "email": "you@work.example" }, { "name": "Daniel Okafor", "email": "daniel@work.example" }],
          "body": "Done. I updated both screens and collapsed older messages in long threads, so the latest reply is always the first thing you read.\n\nOn Wed, You wrote:\n> Every folder, but only the inbox count gets the accent colour.\n> Everything else stays muted so the inbox reads first." }
      ]
    },
